. 
.         * Please add a verbal description of your model here
. 
.         /* Heterogeneity robuts DiD model, following Chaisemartin and D'Hault
> foeuille (2024), for a case with 
>                 staggered and binary treatment. We regress attitudes towards 
> the share of male work in total household work (in hours, during weekdays) 
>                 in a given year on whether a parent has any daughter born bef
> ore attitudes are surveyed, 
>                 controlling for number-of-children-fixed-effects.
>                 Up to four multiple event study effects are estimated. Total 
> average effects are considered.  */
. 
.         xi: did_multiplegt_dyn share_male_housework pid syear any_daughter if
>  sumkids_until_syear > 0, graph_off controls(sumkids_until_syear) effects(4) 


